# Who reviews a change (Step 4.4cc-a). Main's branch rules require a code owner's approval on every pull request, so
# a change merges only after the owner has read it.
#
# Every file here reaches players or decides what reaches them: AzurKit installs what manifest.json lists, the check
# refuses images and keys anywhere in the tree, and LICENSE and NOTICE.md say whose each file is. So the owner owns
# them all.
*                @MichaelJSr

# These four come again last, because the last line that matches a path names its owners. A later line that hands
# a folder to its author (say /variants/<id>/) still can't take them from the owner. Keep them last.
# - manifest.json: the entries, and the sha256 and size AzurKit checks each install against.
# - scripts/: the checker. Pull requests run main's copy (.github/workflows/check.yml).
# - .github/: this file and the pull-request check.
# - .gitattributes: it decides the bytes a checkout writes, and the manifest's sha256s hold only for "* -text".
/manifest.json   @MichaelJSr
/scripts/        @MichaelJSr
/.github/        @MichaelJSr
/.gitattributes  @MichaelJSr
